  "raw_text": "28\n\nAsla lâka ra iwisa\n \n–\n \ndwelling together in unity\n \n/\n \nhabitando juntos en la unidad\n \n(\nhere conjugated as\n \nthird\n\nperson\n \n/\n \na\nquí conjugado como tercera persona\n)\n\nAsla prakaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nAsla prawaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto join unitedly together, to stick together, to meet with\n \n/ unirnos,\nmanterneros juntos, reunirnos con\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb93\n):\n \nJisas ai disaipilka nani ra Galili ra asla prakisa\n \n–\n \nIn Galilee, Jesus meets with his disciples\n \n/\n \nEn Galilea, Jesús se\n\nencuentra con sus discípulos\n)\n\nAsla prawaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nAsla prakaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto join unitedly together, to stick together, to meet with\n \n/ unirnos,\nmanternernos juntos, reunirnos con\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\ndb-Blasi Sturka 2:24\n):\n \nWaitna ba... bara ai mairka ra asla prawbia\n \n–\n \nThe man will stick to his wife\n \n/ El hombre se\nunirá a su esposa)\n\nAsla takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto organize together, to come to be together\n \n/ organizarse juntos, venir a estar juntos\n\n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nAsla aidrubaia\n \n–\n \nto meet together\n \n/ reunirse)\n\nA\nsla takanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \norganizatio\nn, institution\n \n/\n \norganización, institución\n\n(\nEx/\nEj\n(\nmwb\n):\n \nAsla takanka p\nâ\nwanka nani\n \n–\n \nOrganizational Accomplishments\n \n/\n \nLogros de la organización\n \n)\n\nJehova asla takanka\n \n–\n \nJehovah’s organization\n \n/\n \nOrganización de Jehová\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n10/20\n):\n \nSturi yamni smalkaia dukiara, Jehova asla takanka ba d\nî\na\n \ntnatka nani yus munan sa?\n\n–\n \nIn order to preach the good news, what methods has Jehovah’s organization used?\n \n/ Para predicar las\n\nbuenas nuevas, ¿qué\n \nmétodos ha utilizado la organización de Jehová?\n)\n\nJehova asla takanka ra wark nani briaia\n \n–\n \nto have privileges in J\nehovah’s organization\n \n/\ntener privilegios en la organización de Jehová\n\nAsla wark takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto work unitedly together, to work in harmony together, to cooperate\n \n/ trabajar unidos,\ntrabajar en armonía juntos, colaborar, cooperar\n\nAslika ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthe united (group, people...); the unanimous (group, people...)\n \n/\n \nlos unidos (grupo, personas...)\n;\n\nlos unánimes (grupo, personas...)\n\nWal asla\n \n–\n \nunited with, connects with, relates with\n \n/\n \nunido con, conectado con, relacionado con\n\nAsmala\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nnail\n \n(of a finger or\n \ntoe)\n \n/\n \nuña (de un dedo o dedo del pie)\n\n(Construct:\n \nAismala\n;\n \nAmsmala\n;\n \nAi asmala\n)\n\nAspital\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhospital\n \n/\n \nhospital\n\nA\nspital wal Asla Daukaia Daknika\n \n(\nmw\nb\n-\n01/2\n5\n;\n \nhdu\n-\n27\n;\n \nmwb\n-\n01/23\n;\n \na/t:\n \nAspital nani wal Asla\n \nWark Taki ba\n\nKamitika\n-\nmwb\n-\n01/24\n)\n \n–\n \nHospital Liason Committee\n \n(HLC)\n \n/ Comit\né\n \nde Enlace con los Hospitales\n \n(CEH)\n\nAswaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be dying out, to be extinguishing, to be fading\n \n/ extinguirse, desvanecerse\n\nAtia\n \n(adv,adj)\n \n–\n \nall\n \n/ todo\n\nAtkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto sell, to buy, to trade\n \n/ vender, comprar, comerciar\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nAisiki bins atkan\n \n–\n \nmy father sold beans\n \n/ mi padre vendía frijoles )\n\nAtkanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \na selling or buying transaction, the act of selling, the act of buying\n \n/ una transacción de venta o\ncompra, el acto de vender, el acto de comprar\n\nAtki sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto repurchase, to pay a ransom, to ransom\n \n/ recomprar, pagar un rescate, rescatar\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nWitin ai Luhpia yaban atki wan sakaia dukiara\n \n–\n \nHe gave his son to ransom us\n \n/\n \nDio a su hijo\n \npara rescatarnos\n)\n\nAtki sakan lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nAtki sakaia lâka\n-\nkm\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nransom\n \n/ rescate\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nfg\n \ntranslates\n \nransom\n \nas\n \nPri sakaia ba\n;\n \nbh\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia pura mana ba;\n \ndb-Mat20:28\n\ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia mana\n;\n \ndbta-Matiu 20:28\n \ntranslates as\n \nSwaki sakanka mana\n \n/\n \nfg\n \ntraduce\n \nrescate\n \ncomo\n \nPri\nsakaia ba\n;\n \nbh\n \nlo traduce como\n \nPri sakaia pura mana ba\n;\n \ndb-Matiu 20:28\n \nlo traduce como\n \nPri sakaia mana\n;\n \ndbta-\nMatiu 20:28\n \nlo traduce\n \nSwaki sakanka mana\n))\n\nAtki sasakra\n \n(\ndb-Aiseya 48:17\n) (n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nRepurchaser\n \n/ Recomprador\n\nAtki mai sasakra\n \n–\n \nyour Repurchaser\n \n/ tu Recomprador\n\nBrit atkras?\n \n(exp)\n \n–\n \nDo you want to buy bread?; You don’t want to buy\n \nbread?\n \n/ ¿Quieres comprar pan?; ¿No\nquieres comprar pan?\n\nDiara\n \nâ\niatkra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nmerchant,\n \ns\neller, buyer\n \n/\n \ncomerciante, vendedor, comprador\n\n(Construct:\n \nDiara\n \nâiatkriki\n;\n \nDiara\n \nâiatkrikam\n;\n \nDiara\n \nâiatkrika\n)\n\nWauhi\n \nâ\niatkra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nmerchant, seller, buyer\n \n/ comerciante, vendedor, comprador\n\nÂ\nu\n \n(Au)\n \n(\nd\nb,d\nictu\n-\nalt,\ndict\n-\nalt;\n \na/t:\n \nAo\n-\ndict\n,\ndictu\n,\naem\n;\n \nAu\n-\ngpm\n)\n \n–\n \nyes\n \n/\n \ns\ní\n\nÂu sika\n \n(\nÂo sikka\n-\ndict\n)\n \n–\n \nof course, it is so\n \n/ por supuesto, así es\n\nÂu takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto agree\n \n/ aceptar, coincidir, acceder",
